1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,350
Backup reports success: a file exists, the call returned no error.

2
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:11,050
Nothing has been opened. Nothing has been read back.

3
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:15,180
Established: a file was written.

4
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:24,260
Not yet shown: it opens, the links hold, the numbers match.

5
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:33,660
Restore into a fresh path. The source is never overwritten or opened.

6
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:41,500
The copy holds the backup's data, not later source writes.

7
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:47,650
integrity_check → ok.  foreign_key_check → no rows.

8
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:55,550
Different questions. Passing one does not answer the other.

9
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:59,970
12 customers, 40 orders. Known values match.

10
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:06,910
The app's real order-total query: 12 of 12 totals as expected.

11
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:17,450
Invalid artifacts fail validation with a structured result, not a crash.

12
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:28,000
Same counts can still hide an orphan or a wrong value.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,040
One small synthetic database. No recovery-time or recovery-point claim.

14
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:38,950
The restore is the test.
